{"title": "Q3 Design Studio Quarterly Review", "theme": "editorial", "slides": [
  {
    "title": "Key Highlights",
    "bullets": [
      "Completed 12 client projects, up 20% from Q2",
      "Launched new brand identity for [Client Name] – awarded 'Best New Brand' at local design festival",
      "Reduced project delivery time by 15% through streamlined workflow tools",
      "Increased client retention to 85% (up from 70% in Q2)"
    ],
    "notes": "We delivered strong results across both volume and quality. The new brand win reflects our growing reputation in niche markets. Time savings came from adopting a standardized design template library and better task delegation.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  },
  {
    "title": "Performance Metrics",
    "bullets": [
      "Avg. project revenue: $4,200 (up 10% from Q2)",
      "Client satisfaction score: 4.7/5 (improved from 4.3)",
      "Project completion rate: 96% (vs. 92% last quarter)"
    ],
    "notes": "Revenue growth reflects both increased volume and higher average project value. Satisfaction scores indicate improved communication and delivery consistency. Completion rate improvement shows better project planning and follow-up.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  },
  {
    "title": "Key Lessons Learned",
    "bullets": [
      "Clear scope definition upfront prevents scope creep and rework",
      "Client feedback loops must be integrated early and regularly",
      "Team capacity is limited—overcommitting leads to burnout and delays"
    ],
    "notes": "We saw repeated delays when projects started without defined deliverables. Early feedback sessions helped catch misalignments before they escalated. We now schedule a weekly check-in with clients to maintain alignment.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  },
  {
    "title": "Next Quarter Focus",
    "bullets": [
      "Launch new service: UX audits for startups (target: 5 new clients)",
      "Implement project tracking dashboard to improve visibility and forecasting",
      "Host a client workshop to strengthen long-term relationships"
    ],
    "notes": "This quarter will focus on scaling our expertise in early-stage user experience. The dashboard will help us predict workload and avoid overbooking. Workshops will build trust and deepen engagement beyond one-off projects.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  }
]}

{"title": "Welcome to Our Volunteer Programme", "theme": "editorial", "slides": [
  {
    "title": "Welcome!",
    "bullets": [
      "We're thrilled you're joining our volunteer team",
      "Your passion and time make a real difference",
      "You'll be part of a supportive, inclusive community",
      "Everyone starts with a warm welcome and clear onboarding"
    ],
    "notes": "Start with warmth and enthusiasm. Emphasize that every volunteer brings unique value. Reassure them they’re not alone—support is built in from day one.",
    "layout": "title"
  },
  {
    "title": "What You’ll Do",
    "bullets": [
      "Support events and outreach activities",
      "Assist with community engagement and communications",
      "Help manage logistics like setup, cleanup, and guest support",
      "Learn new skills through hands-on experience"
    ],
    "notes": "Be specific but flexible—highlight variety without overpromising. Stress learning and growth as part of the experience.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  },
  {
    "title": "How Shifts Work",
    "bullets": [
      "Shifts are scheduled weekly via our shared calendar",
      "Volunteers can choose from pre-set times or request flexibility",
      "Shifts last 2–4 hours, with clear start/end times",
      "All shifts are confirmed in advance with a brief check-in"
    ],
    "notes": "Clarify that shifts are flexible but require advance notice. Mention the calendar is accessible to all volunteers. Keep it simple and practical.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  },
  {
    "title": "Who to Ask",
    "bullets": [
      "Contact the Volunteer Coordinator at [email address]",
      "Reach out to your assigned buddy during onboarding",
      "Ask questions at any event or shift briefing"
    ],
    "notes": "Make it easy to find support. Highlight the buddy system as a key resource. Encourage proactive questions—no one should feel unsure.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  },
  {
    "title": "First Steps",
    "bullets": [
      "Complete the online onboarding form by [date]",
      "Attend the welcome session on [date and time]",
      "Sign up for your first shift via the volunteer portal",
      "Meet your buddy and get a welcome kit"
    ],
    "notes": "Provide clear, actionable next steps. Emphasize that the first few days are designed to ease into the role. Keep it structured but friendly.",
    "layout": "title-content"
  }
]}
